#!/usr/bin/env python3

"""
UDCPR CLEAN POSTGRESQL REBUILD

Purpose
-------
Rebuild the UDCPR PostgreSQL tables from the canonical source chunks.

IMPORTANT
---------
This script intentionally DOES NOT attempt to repair/match the existing
PostgreSQL "tables" records.

Source of truth:

    data/regulations/udcpr_canonical_manifest.json
    data/regulations/udcpr_source_chunks.json

The existing PostgreSQL tables table is preserved by renaming it to:

    tables_backup_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS

Then a completely new public.tables table is created.

The existing regulations table is NOT modified.

The new tables are created directly from the canonical source chunks.

Expected source:

    329 canonical regulations
    329 source chunks
    1087 source tables

Dry-run:
    No PostgreSQL changes.

Apply:
    One PostgreSQL transaction.

Example
-------
python tools/rebuild_udcpr_database.py \
    --manifest data/regulations/udcpr_canonical_manifest.json \
    --chunks data/regulations/udcpr_source_chunks.json \
    --report /tmp/udcpr_full_rebuild.json

Actual:
    add --apply
"""

